SZ="fair_ia_sein_und_zeit.txt"
q("t-sinn-bedeutung","Es liegt nun nahe, mit einem Zeichen (Namen, Wortverbindung, Schriftzeichen) außer dem Bezeichneten, was die Bedeutung des Zeichens heißen möge, noch das verbunden zu denken, was ich den Sinn des Zeichens nennen möchte, worin die Art des Gegebenseins enthalten ist.","It is natural to think of a sign (name, phrase, written mark) as connected not only with what it designates, which may be called its reference, but also with what I would like to call its sense, in which the mode of presentation is contained.","Über Sinn und Bedeutung","1892, p. 26","ia_frege_sinn_und_bedeutung.txt")
q("t-gedanke","Ich verstehe unter Gedanken nicht das subjektive Tun des Denkens, sondern dessen objektiven Inhalt, der fähig ist, gemeinsames Eigentum von vielen zu sein.","By a thought I understand not the subjective act of thinking but its objective content, which is capable of being the common property of many.","Über Sinn und Bedeutung","1892, p. 32 n.","ia_frege_sinn_und_bedeutung.txt")
q("t-begriffsschrift","Hieraus ergab sich auch der Name „Begriffsschrift\".","Hence too the name 'concept-script'.","Begriffsschrift","1879, Preface","ia_11388662.txt")
q("t-weltanschauung","dessen Idee eines Noumenons, welches selbst keine Anschauung verstattet, aber doch der Weltanschauung, als bloßer Erscheinung, zum Substrat untergelegt wird","the idea of a noumenon, which itself admits of no intuition but is laid down as the substrate of our intuition of the world as mere appearance.","Kritik der Urteilskraft","§ 26 (AA V, 255)","kk_aa05_255.txt")
q("t-zeitgeist","Was das Individuum betrifft, so ist ohnehin jedes ein Sohn seiner Zeit; so ist auch die Philosophie ihre Zeit in Gedanken erfaßt.","As for the individual, each is in any case a child of his time; so philosophy too is its own time comprehended in thought.","Grundlinien der Philosophie des Rechts","Preface","ia_grundlinienderph00hege.txt")
q("t-dasein","Das Dasein ist ein Seiendes, das nicht nur unter anderem Seienden vorkommt. Es ist vielmehr dadurch ontisch ausgezeichnet, daß es diesem Seienden in seinem Sein um dieses Sein selbst geht.","Dasein is an entity that does not just occur among other entities. Rather, it is ontically distinguished by the fact that, in its very being, that being is an issue for it.","Sein und Zeit","§ 4, p. 12",SZ)
q("t-in-der-welt-sein","Der zusammengesetzte Ausdruck »In-der-Welt-sein« zeigt schon in seiner Prägung an, daß mit ihm ein einheitliches Phänomen gemeint ist.","The compound expression 'being-in-the-world' shows in its very coinage that it stands for a unitary phenomenon.","Sein und Zeit","§ 12, p. 53",SZ)
q("t-sein-zum-tode","Der Tod ist eine Weise zu sein, die das Dasein übernimmt, sobald es ist.","Death is a way to be, which Dasein takes over as soon as it is.","Sein und Zeit","§ 48, p. 245",SZ)
q("t-das-man","Jeder ist der Andere und Keiner er selbst.","Everyone is the other, and no one is himself.","Sein und Zeit","§ 27, p. 128",SZ)
q("t-sorge","Das Sein des Daseins besagt: Sich-vorweg-schon-sein-in-(der-Welt-) als Sein-bei (innerweltlich begegnendem Seienden).","The being of Dasein means: ahead-of-itself-already-being-in-(the-world) as being-alongside (entities encountered within the world).","Sein und Zeit","§ 41, p. 192",SZ)
q("t-geworfenheit","Diesen in seinem Woher und Wohin verhüllten, aber an ihm selbst um so unverhüllter erschlossenen Seinscharakter des Daseins, dieses »Daß es ist« nennen wir die Geworfenheit dieses Seienden in sein Da","This character of Dasein's being, veiled in its whence and whither but disclosed all the more unveiledly in itself, this 'that it is', we call the thrownness of this entity into its 'there'.","Sein und Zeit","§ 29, p. 135",SZ)
q("t-zuhanden","Die Seinsart von Zeug, in der es sich von ihm selbst her offenbart, nennen wir die Zuhandenheit.","The kind of being of equipment, in which it manifests itself in its own right, we call readiness-to-hand.","Sein und Zeit","§ 15, p. 69",SZ)
q("t-verfallen","Das Dasein ist von ihm selbst als eigentlichem Selbstseinkönnen zunächst immer schon abgefallen und an die »Welt« verfallen.","Dasein has, proximally, always already fallen away from itself as an authentic potentiality for being itself, and has fallen into the 'world'.","Sein und Zeit","§ 38, p. 175",SZ)
q("t-eigentlichkeit","Und weil Dasein wesenhaft je seine Möglichkeit ist, kann dieses Seiende in seinem Sein sich selbst »wählen«, gewinnen, es kann sich verlieren","And because Dasein is in each case essentially its possibility, it can, in its very being, 'choose' itself and win itself; it can also lose itself.","Sein und Zeit","§ 9, p. 42",SZ)
q("t-ontologische-differenz","Das Sein des Seienden »ist« nicht selbst ein Seiendes.","The being of entities 'is' not itself an entity.","Sein und Zeit","§ 2, p. 6",SZ)
q("t-aletheia","Seiendes – aus der Verborgenheit herausnehmend – in seiner Unverborgenheit (Entdecktheit) sehen lassen","letting entities be seen in their unconcealment (uncoveredness), taking them out of concealment.","Sein und Zeit","§ 44, p. 219",SZ)
q("t-lichtung","Es ist »erleuchtet«, besagt: an ihm selbst als In-der-Welt-sein gelichtet, nicht durch ein anderes Seiendes, sondern so, daß es selbst die Lichtung ist.","To say it is 'illuminated' means: lit up in itself as being-in-the-world, not by some other entity, but in such a way that it is itself the clearing.","Sein und Zeit","§ 28, p. 133",SZ)
q("t-seinsvergessenheit","Die genannte Frage ist heute in Vergessenheit gekommen, obzwar unsere Zeit sich als Fortschritt anrechnet, die »Metaphysik« wieder zu bejahen.","This question has today been forgotten, although our time counts it as progress to affirm 'metaphysics' again.","Sein und Zeit","§ 1, p. 2",SZ)
q("t-gestell","Der Name für die Versammlung des Herausforderns, das Mensch und Sein einander so zu-stellt, daß sie sich wechselweise stellen, lautet: das Ge-Stell.","The name for the gathering of this challenge, which sets man and being upon each other so that they challenge each other in turn, is: the Ge-Stell.","Identität und Differenz","'Der Satz der Identität' (1957)","fair_ia_identitaet_und_differenz.txt")
q("t-ereignis","Er-eignen heißt ursprünglich: er-äugen, d. h. erblicken, im Blicken zu sich rufen, an-eignen. … Als so gedachtes Leitwort läßt es sich sowenig übersetzen wie das griechische Leitwort λόγος und das chinesische Tao.","Er-eignen originally means: to catch with the eye, i.e. to glimpse, to call to oneself in looking, to appropriate. … Thought as such a guide-word, it can no more be translated than the Greek guide-word logos or the Chinese Tao.","Identität und Differenz","'Der Satz der Identität' (1957)","fair_ia_identitaet_und_differenz.txt")
q("t-absurde","L'absurde naît de cette confrontation entre l'appel humain et le silence déraisonnable du monde.","The absurd is born of this confrontation between the human call and the unreasonable silence of the world.","Le Mythe de Sisyphe","'Les murs absurdes'","fair_ia_mythe_sisyphe.txt")
q("t-deuxieme-sexe","On ne naît pas femme : on le devient.","One is not born, but rather becomes, a woman.","Le Deuxième Sexe II","Part I, ch. 1, opening","fair_ia_deuxieme_sexe2.txt")
q("t-deconstruction","Il n'y a pas de hors-texte.","There is no outside-text.","De la grammatologie","Minuit 1967, p. 227","fair_ia_grammatologie.txt")
q("t-trace","La trace n'est pas seulement la disparition de l'origine, elle veut dire ici … que l'origine n'a même pas disparu, qu'elle n'a jamais été constituée qu'en retour par une non-origine","The trace is not only the disappearance of origin; it means here … that the origin did not even disappear, that it was never constituted except reciprocally by a non-origin.","De la grammatologie","Minuit 1967, p. 90","fair_ia_grammatologie.txt")
q("t-differance","la différance, concept économique désignant la production du différer, au double sens de ce mot.","différance, an economic concept designating the production of deferring/differing, in the double sense of that word.","De la grammatologie","Minuit 1967, p. 38","fair_ia_grammatologie.txt")
q("t-simulacre","Le simulacre n'est jamais ce qui cache la vérité – c'est la vérité qui cache qu'il n'y en a pas. Le simulacre est vrai.","The simulacrum is never what hides the truth: it is the truth that hides that there is none. The simulacrum is true.","Simulacres et simulation","Galilée 1981, p. 9 (epigraph)","fair_ia_simulacres.txt")
q("t-episteme-foucault","Dans une culture et à un moment donné, il n'y a jamais qu'une épistémè, qui définit les conditions de possibilité de tout savoir.","In any given culture and at any given moment, there is only ever one episteme, which defines the conditions of possibility of all knowledge.","Les Mots et les choses","ch. VI, p. 179","fair_ia_mots_et_choses.txt")
q("t-pouvoir-savoir","pouvoir et savoir s'impliquent directement l'un l'autre","power and knowledge directly imply one another.","Surveiller et punir","Part I, ch. 1, p. 32","fair_ia_surveiller_punir.txt")
q("t-bricolage","la règle de son jeu est de toujours s'arranger avec les « moyens du bord »","the rule of his game is always to make do with 'whatever is at hand'.","La Pensée sauvage","ch. 1, p. 27","fair_ia_pensee_sauvage.txt")
q("t-habitus","habitus, systèmes de dispositions durables, structures structurées prédisposées à fonctionner comme structures structurantes","habitus: systems of durable dispositions, structured structures predisposed to function as structuring structures.","Esquisse d'une théorie de la pratique","'Structures, habitus et pratiques'","fair_ia_esquisse.txt")
q("t-jouissance","la jouissance est interdite à qui parle comme tel, ou encore qu'elle ne puisse être dite qu'entre les lignes pour quiconque est sujet de la Loi","jouissance is forbidden to whoever speaks as such, or else it can be said only between the lines by whoever is subject of the Law.","Écrits","'Subversion du sujet', p. 821","fair_ia_ecrits.txt")
q("t-objet-a","ce qui se lève à la fin de ce recueil sous le nom d'objet a (à lire : petit a)","what rises at the end of this collection under the name of object a (to be read: little a).","Écrits","'Ouverture de ce recueil', p. 10","fair_ia_ecrits.txt")
q("t-mauvaise-foi","Considérons ce garçon de café. … il joue à être garçon de café","Let us consider this café waiter. … he is playing at being a café waiter.","L'Être et le néant","Part I, ch. 2, § II","fair_ia_etre_neant.txt")
q("t-pour-soi","Dire que le pour-soi a à être ce qu'il est, dire qu'il est ce qu'il n'est pas en n'étant pas ce qu'il est","To say that the for-itself has to be what it is, to say that it is what it is not while not being what it is.","L'Être et le néant","Part IV, ch. 1","fair_ia_etre_neant.txt")
q("t-engagement","Je suis condamné à exister pour toujours par delà mon essence, par delà les mobiles et les motifs de mon acte : je suis condamné à être libre.","I am condemned to exist forever beyond my essence, beyond the causes and motives of my act: I am condemned to be free.","L'Être et le néant","Part IV, ch. 1","fair_ia_etre_neant.txt")
q("t-existence-precede","L'existence précède l'essence.","Existence precedes essence.","L'existentialisme est un humanisme","Nagel 1970, p. 17","fair_wq_fr_Sartre.txt")
q("t-visage","le visage est ce qui nous interdit de tuer.","the face is what forbids us to kill.","Éthique et Infini","Livre de poche 1982, p. 80","fair_wq_fr_Levinas.txt")
q("t-il-y-a","Dans le vide absolu, qu'on peut imaginer, d'avant la création — il y a.","In the absolute void that one can imagine, before creation: there is.","Éthique et Infini","Livre de poche 1982, p. 38","fair_wq_fr_Levinas.txt")
q("t-epoche-husserl","Die zum Wesen der natürlichen Einstellung gehörige Generalthesis setzen wir außer Aktion, alles und jedes, was sie in ontischer Hinsicht umspannt, setzen wir in Klammern","We put out of action the general thesis belonging to the essence of the natural attitude; everything it encompasses in the ontic respect we place in brackets.","Ideen I","§ 32","ia_jppf1.1.txt")
q("t-noesis-noema","Überall entspricht den mannigfaltigen Daten des reellen, noetischen Gehaltes eine Mannigfaltigkeit in wirklich reiner Intuition aufweisbarer Daten … Die Wahrnehmung z. B. hat ihr Noema","Everywhere the manifold data of the real, noetic content correspond to a manifold of data demonstrable in actually pure intuition … Perception, for example, has its noema.","Ideen I","§ 88","ia_jppf1.1.txt")
q("t-lebenswelt","die wirklich wahrnehmungsmäßig gegebene … erfahrbare Welt – unsere alltägliche Lebenswelt","the world actually given in perception … the experienceable world: our everyday life-world.","Die Krisis der europäischen Wissenschaften","§ 9h","fair_lebenswelt_art.txt")
q("t-wiener-kreis","Die wissenschaftliche Weltauffassung kennt keine unlösbaren Rätsel.","The scientific world-conception knows no unsolvable riddles.","Wissenschaftliche Weltauffassung. Der Wiener Kreis","1929, § II","fair_wk.txt")
q("t-klassenbewusstsein","Ainsi cette masse est déjà une classe vis-à-vis du capital, mais pas encore pour elle-même. Dans la lutte, … cette masse se réunit, elle se constitue en classe pour elle-même.","Thus this mass is already a class as against capital, but not yet for itself. In the struggle … this mass unites and constitutes itself as a class for itself.","Misère de la philosophie","ch. II, § 5","misere.txt")
q("t-aspektsehen","Dieses Gesicht (das den Eindruck der Furchtsamkeit macht) kann ich mir auch als ein mutiges denken. … Ich rede vielmehr von einem Aspekt des Gesichtes selbst.","I can also think of this face (which gives an impression of timidity) as a courageous one. … Rather, I am speaking of an aspect of the face itself.","Philosophische Untersuchungen","§ 536","pi.html")
q("t-imago-dei","Ecce ergo mens meminit sui, intellegit se, diligit se: hoc si cernimus, cernimus trinitatem; nondum quidem Deum, sed iam imaginem Dei.","See, then: the mind remembers itself, understands itself, loves itself. If we discern this, we discern a trinity: not yet God, but already the image of God.","De Trinitate","XIV.8.11","trin14.txt")
q("t-universalia","ipsa enim genera et species subsistunt quidem alio modo, intelleguntur uero alio, et sunt incorporalia, sed sensibilibus iuncta subsistunt in sensibilibus","genera and species themselves subsist in one way but are understood in another; they are incorporeal, yet, joined to sensible things, they subsist in sensible things.","In Isagogen Porphyrii, ed. secunda","I.11 (CSEL 48, p. 167)","ia_aniciimanliiseue48boet.txt")
q("t-occams-razor","ipsa substantia sine omni alia re absoluta, totaliter distincta, formaliter inhaerente, est quanta et corpus. Igitur superfluum est talem rem aliam ponere sibi inhaerentem.","substance itself, without any other absolute thing wholly distinct from it and formally inhering in it, is quantified and a body. So it is superfluous to posit such another thing inhering in it.","Expositio in librum Praedicamentorum","on quantity (OPh II, p. 210)","ia_william-of-ockham-opera-philosophica-vol-2.txt")
q("t-gelassenheit","Der mensche, der gelâzen hât unde gelâzen ist unde nie mêr gesiht einen blik ûf daz, daz er gelâzen hât, unde stæte und unbewegt blîbet und unwandellîche in ime selber, der mensche ist alleine gelâzen.","The person who has let go and is let go, and never again casts a glance at what he has let go, and stays steady, unmoved and unchanging in himself: that person alone is released.","Predigt XCVI","Pfeiffer, Deutsche Mystiker II, p. 312","ia_deutschemystiker02pfei.txt")
q("t-haecceitas","Non est igitur 'ista entitas' materia vel forma vel compositum, in quantum quodlibet istorum est 'natura', - sed est ultima realitas entis quod est materia vel quod est forma","So 'this entity' is not matter or form or the composite, insofar as each of these is a 'nature', but it is the ultimate reality of the being that is matter or that is form.","Ordinatio II","d. 3, p. 1, q. 6, n. 188","scotus_ord2d3q6.txt")
q("t-potentia-absoluta","Credo in Deum Patrem omnipotentem, quem sic intelligo: quod quodlibet est divinae potentiae attribuendum, quod non includit manifestam contradictionem","I believe in God the Father almighty, which I understand thus: anything is to be attributed to the divine power that does not involve a manifest contradiction.","Quodlibeta","VI, q. 6","ia_boehner_ockham.txt")
q("t-tahafut","الاقتران بين ما يعتقد في العادة سببا وما يعتقد مسببا ليس ضروريا عندنا","The connection between what is customarily believed to be a cause and what is believed to be an effect is not necessary, in our view.","Tahāfut al-falāsifa","17th discussion","oi_0505Ghazali.Tahafut.clean.txt")
q("t-falsafa","أن نفحص، على جهة النظر الشرعي، هل النظر في الفلسفة وعلوم المنطق مباح بالشرع، أم محظور، أم مأمور به","[The aim of this treatise is] to examine, from the standpoint of religious law, whether the study of philosophy and the sciences of logic is permitted by the Law, forbidden, or commanded.","Faṣl al-maqāl","opening","oi_0595IbnRushdHafid.FaslMaqal.clean.txt")
q("t-wujud","فإن لكل أمر حقيقة هو بها ما هو، فالمثلث حقيقة أنه مثلث، وللبياض حقيقة أنه بياض، وذلك هو الذي ربما سميناه الوجود الخاص","For each thing has a reality by which it is what it is: the triangle has the reality of being a triangle, whiteness the reality of being whiteness; and this is what we have perhaps called its proper existence.","al-Shifāʾ: al-Ilāhiyyāt","I.5","oi_0428IbnSina.ShifaIlahiyyat.clean.txt")
q("t-dike","διδόναι γὰρ αὐτὰ δίκην καὶ τίσιν ἀλλήλοις τῆς ἀδικίας κατὰ τὴν τοῦ χρόνου τάξιν","for they pay penalty and retribution to one another for their injustice according to the ordering of time.","Anaximander, fragment B1 (via Simplicius)","in Phys. 24.13–21","wp_en_Anaximander.txt")
